course: dictionary
lesson: 12230
title: Conserves: jam or saving?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word conserves has two meanings, so read the words around it to find out which one fits. «Grandma spread her homemade conserves on warm toast.» Here conserves are jams made from whole fruit pieces cooked with sugar.
explain: As a verb, conserves means saves, protects or uses carefully so nothing is wasted. «Ella conserves water by turning off the tap while she brushes her teeth.» Ella is not throwing water away. She is saving it.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. «Ella saves water by turning off the tap while she brushes her teeth» still makes sense, so conserves means saves in this sentence. «Grandma spread her homemade saves on warm toast» does not make sense, so this sentence needs the jam meaning.
explain: Look for the little clues. He conserves and she conserves are the verb form, and the sentence will be about doing something. Conserves with a jar, toast or spoon is usually the jam. «The ranger conserves the forest, so the owls keep their homes.»
fact: Conserves (noun) means jams made from whole fruit pieces cooked with sugar.
fact: Conserves (verb) means saves, protects or uses carefully so it is not wasted.
fact: He or she conserves something: «Sam conserves his pocket money for a new bike.»
fact: Useful phrases: conserves energy, conserves water, conserves habitats (the homes of plants and animals).
fact: In science, energy is conserved: the total amount stays the same, even when it changes from one form into another.
exercise: «Grandma spread her homemade conserves on warm toast.» In this sentence, what are conserves? | Sad songs | Tiny boats | Old shoes | *Jams made from fruit cooked with sugar
exercise: «The farmer conserves water by fixing the leaking pipe.» What does conserves mean here? | Throws it away | *Saves it so none is wasted | Freezes it solid | Splashes it everywhere
exercise: «Mia conserves her energy for the last race.» What does conserves mean? | *Saves it so it lasts | Spends it all at once | Hides it under the bed | Shouts it loudly
test: «Ben conserves paper by printing on both sides.» What does conserves mean here? | Sells in the shop | Wastes | *Saves and uses carefully | Burns
test: «Dad opened a jar of plum conserves for breakfast.» What are conserves in this sentence? | Old bread | Cold soup | *Jams made from fruit cooked with sugar | Paper bags
exam: Which sentence uses conserves as a verb (a doing word)? | Dad loves strawberry conserves | Mum put the conserves on the table | Jars of conserves sit in the cupboard | *The class conserves energy by switching off unused lights
